Design a room plan page for a hotel management system with the following features and layout:
1. Page Structure:
   - The page should be divided into three main sections:
     - Room List
     - Unassigned Guest List
     - Legend
   - Each section should be collapsible (Accordion) and vertically resizable.

2. Room List:
   - At the top of the page, include a date picker that allows users to select a starting date. The calendar sections will display data for the next 7 days from the selected date.
   - have 1 table that contains room information and calendar for each row
   - room information:
     - Display key details for each room: 
       - Room Number
       - Room Type
       - (On Hover) Show additional Room Status Details, including:
         - Room Number
         - Room Type & Description
         - Floor
         - Exposure
         - Room Attributes
         - Smoking (yes/no)
         - Clean (yes/no)
   - calendar have:
     - Include a Room Reservation Gantt Chart that visualizes reservations.
     - Implement an Item Card system where each item card can occupy one or more cells in the Gantt Chart.
       - Each Item Card should display the guest name.
       - On Hover: Show Reservation Details card including:
         - Room Number + Guest Name
         - Confirmation Number
         - Arrival Date
         - Departure Date
         - Adult
         - Rate
         - Rate Plan
         - Folio Balance
         - Settlement Type
         - Booking Agency
     - Each Item Card should support drag & drop functionality to move reservations between rooms.
     - Allow users to shorten or lengthen Item Cards to adjust reservation dates.
     - Implement a locking feature: locked items should not be movable or resizable.
 
3. Unassigned Guest List: This section is to be determined (TBA); further specifications will be provided later.

4. Legend: This section is to be determined (TBA); further specifications will be provided later.

5. Design Considerations:
   - Ensure a clean user interface that promotes usability.
   - Use visual cues to differentiate between different room types and reservation statuses.
   - Include icons to represent different actions (e.g., drag-and-drop, locked status, etc.).
